<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Chocolatey package for da-mcp — Desktop Automation MCP Server.

    Build:    choco pack
    Install:  choco install da-mcp -s .
    Push:     choco push da-mcp.0.1.0.nupkg -s https://push.chocolatey.org/

    The .nupkg is generated by `choco pack` from this .nuspec + the files
    referenced under <files>. See packaging/chocolatey/README.md for details.

    Update <version>, <checksum>, and the download URL together when
    releasing a new version.
-->
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>da-mcp</id>
    <version>0.1.0</version>
    <title>da-mcp — Desktop Automation MCP Server</title>
    <authors>cioinside</authors>
    <owners>cioinside</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/cioinside/da-mcp</projectUrl>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/cioinside/da-mcp/tree/main/packaging/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/cioinside/da-mcp/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cioinside/da-mcp/main/packaging/icon.png</iconUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/cioinside/da-mcp/blob/main/README.md</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/cioinside/da-mcp/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <summary>Cross-platform desktop automation MCP server (12 tools: screenshot, OCR, mouse, keyboard, launch).</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
da-mcp is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets AI agents
(OpenCode, Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.) interact with a local desktop
environment on Linux, macOS, and Windows.

12 tools registered under the `da_*` namespace:

* Capture:  da_screenshot, da_ocr, da_list_displays
* Input:    da_get_mouse_position, da_move_mouse, da_click,
            da_double_click, da_drag, da_scroll, da_type, da_key
* Launch:   da_launch

Highlights
* Cross-platform: Linux (X11 + Wayland), macOS, Windows
* Screenshot dispatch: node-screenshots → screenshot-desktop →
  PowerShell BitBlt fallback on Windows
* OCR via tesseract CLI (primary) or tesseract.js WASM (fallback)
* UI element classification: button / input / label / checkbox / radio
  / menu / menu-item / icon
* Input: xdotool / ydotool / wtype (Linux) · @nut-tree-fork/nut-js (macOS / Windows)
* Strict TypeScript + ESM, 250 LOC per file ceiling, 216 passing tests

After install, point your MCP client at:
  node "<INSTALLDIR>\tools\da-mcp\dist\server.js"

Full documentation: https://github.com/cioinside/da-mcp
]]></description>
    <tags>mcp desktop-automation screenshot ocr tesseract mouse keyboard linux windows macos nodejs</tags>
    <copyright>MIT © ciouside</copyright>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="nodejs-lts" version="22.0.0" />
      <dependency id="tesseract" version="5.0.0" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <files>
    <!-- tools/* is added automatically based on the layout in this folder -->
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
